\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Foundational Confession: The One God\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Deuteronomy 6:4 \'97 The Shema\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And these are the statutes and the judgments, which the Lord commanded to the sons of Israel in the wilderness as they were coming out from the land of Egypt. Hear, O Israel: The Lord our God is one Lord. \'97 
\f0\b Deuteronomy 6:4, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the bedrock confession. 
\f0\b One Lord. One God.
\f2\b0  Not three. Not a council. Not a composite 
\f1\i (a mixture of parts made into one)
\f2\i0 . 
\f0\b One.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Second witness \'97 from the lips of the Messiah Himself:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Jesus answered him, The first of all the commandments is, Hear, Israel, The Lord our God is the only Lord. \'97 
\f0\b Mark 12:29, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 A HISTORICAL NOTE:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i Nicaea \'97 the council called by Emperor Constantine in A.D. 325 \'97 is where the \'93same substance\'94 
\f2\i0 (homoousios)
\f1\i  language for the Son was first pressed upon the churches; the fully-worded \'93three persons, one essence\'94 creed followed at Constantinople, A.D. 381. That is the framework this study weighs against the Scripture itself.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus Himself \'97 centuries after Moses, and yet centuries before Nicaea \'97 affirms the Shema 
\f1\i (Hebrew, \'93hear\'94 \'97 the name of Israel\'92s one-God confession)
\f2\i0  as the 
\f0\b first
\f2\b0  of all commandments. He does not amend it. He does not qualify it. He confesses 
\f0\b one God
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Father Identified as That One God\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Witness #1 \'97 Jesus to the Father:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And this is life eternal, that they know thee to be the only very God 
\f1\i (the only true God)
\f2\i0 , and whom thou hast sent, Jesus Christ. \'97 
\f0\b John 17:3, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Messiah Himself addresses the Father as 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 "the only true God" \'97 and distinguishes Himself, 
\f0\b \uc0\u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0 , as the one 
\f1\i sent
\f2\i0  by that God. The Sender and the Sent are not collapsed; the One God is the Father, and Jesus is His Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Witness #2 \'97 Paul to the Corinthians:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Yet unto us there is but one God, which is that Father, of whom are all things, and we in him: and one Lord Jesus Christ, by whom are all things, and we by him. \'97 
\f0\b 1 Corinthians 8:6, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Paul, the Apostle, places 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u942 \u961 
\f2\b0  \'97 the Father \'97 as the 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7990 \u962  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0 , the 
\f1\i one
\f2\i0  God. Jesus Christ is named 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7990 \u962  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i one Lord
\f2\i0  \'97 the agent 
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \'92 \u959 \u8023 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (through whom)
\f2\i0 . The Father is the Source (
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u958  \u959 \u8023 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i of whom
\f2\i0 ); the Son is the Mediator/Instrument 
\f1\i (the one standing between, the one through whom He works)
\f2\i0  (
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \'92 \u959 \u8023 
\f2\b0 ).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Two witnesses established: The One God of the Shema is the Father. Jesus the Christ is His Sent One, His Anointed, His Lord \'97 distinct from the One God, and subordinate 
\f3\i (in ordered rank beneath Him)
\f0\i0  as the agent to the Source.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Further Confirmation From the Mouth of the Son\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 John 20:17:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Jesus saith unto her, Touch me not: for I am not yet ascended to my Father: but go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and to your Father, and to my God, and your God. \'97 
\f0\b John 20:17, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Even after the resurrection, Jesus calls the Father 
\f0\b \uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u957  \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i my God
\f2\i0 . The Risen Christ has a God. That God is the Father.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Ephesians 1:17 \'97 Paul agrees:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, that Father of glory, might give unto you the Spirit of wisdom, and revelation through the acknowledging of him 
\f1\i (truly knowing him)
\f2\i0 , \'97 
\f0\b Ephesians 1:17, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Two witnesses: 
\f0\b The Father is the God 
\f3\i of
\f0\i0  Jesus Christ.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Therefore, our refined foundation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 1. There is 
\f0\b one God
\f2\b0  \'97 Deut. 6:4, confirmed by Jesus in Mark 12:29.\
2. That one God is 
\f0\b the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 John 17:3, 1 Cor. 8:6.\
3. Jesus the Christ is the 
\f0\b Son
\f2\b0  of that God, the 
\f0\b sent
\f2\b0  one, the 
\f0\b Lord
\f2\b0  through whom the Father acts \'97 distinct from, and having as His own God, the Father.\
4. The "Spirit of God" in Genesis 1:2 must therefore be understood not as a separate "person" of a later-invented triune 
\f1\i (three-persons)
\f2\i0  godhead 
\f1\i (see the Historical Note at Mark 12:29)
\f2\i0 , but according to its plain Scriptural usage \'97 which we will examine in due course as 
\f0\b the breath, power, and active presence of the One God Himself
\f2\b0  (cf. Ps 32:6 LXX \'97 
\f1\i "By the word of the Lord the heavens were made firm, and by the breath of his mouth all their host"
\f2\i0  \'97 where the 
\f1\i word
\f2\i0  and the 
\f1\i breath of His mouth
\f2\i0  are instrumental 
\f1\i (the means He uses)
\f2\i0  expressions of the one Lord).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Now \'97 returning to Genesis 1:1 in light of this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 In the beginning God made the sky and the earth. \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 1:1, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (the God)
\f2\i0  here is 
\f0\b the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 the one God of the Shema. He is the Creator. He is the Source (
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u958  \u959 \u8023  \u964 \u8048  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945 
\f2\b0 , 1 Cor 8:6).\
The question we will need to address carefully \'97 without trinitarian assumptions \'97 is the relationship of the 
\f0\b Son
\f2\b0  to this creative act, given that 1 Cor 8:6 also says 
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \'92 \u959 \u8023  \u964 \u8048  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945 
\f2\b0  ("by whom are all things") of Jesus Christ, and that John 1:1-3 speaks of the 
\f0\b \uc0\u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0 .\
That investigation belongs to the 
\f0\b Son's
\f2\b0  part of the study, and we will undertake it only 
\f1\i after
\f2\i0  the Father \'97 the One God \'97 is firmly established as the foundation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 ISAIAH 44 \'97 "Beside Me there is no God"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Isaiah 44-46 contains some of the most thunderous, uncompromising declarations of monotheism 
\f1\i (the teaching that there is one God)
\f2\i0  in all of Scripture. The One God speaks for Himself here \'97 in the first person \'97 and leaves no room for any rival, partner, council, or co-equal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 44:6\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Thus says God, the king of Israel, who delivered him, God Sabaoth 
\f1\i (Hebrew, "of the armies" \'97 the Lord of hosts)
\f2\i0 : I am first, and I am after these things; besides me there is no god. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 44:6, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Observation:
\f2\b0  The speaker \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0 , the King of Israel, the Redeemer, the Lord of Hosts \'97 declares: 
\f0\b "I am first, and I am after these things; besides me there is no god."
\f2\b0  Not "no other God like Me," not "no God of equal rank" \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (a god there is not)
\f2\i0 . There is no God. Full stop.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 44:8\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Do not cover yourselves; did you not give ear 
\f1\i (listen)
\f2\i0  from the beginning, and I declared it to you? You are witnesses whether there is a god 
\f1\i (any god)
\f2\i0  besides me, and they were not formerly. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 44:8, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Observation:
\f2\b0  The God of Israel calls His people as 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u940 \u961 \u964 \u965 \u961 \u949 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i witnesses
\f2\i0  \'97 to testify whether any other god exists. His own answer: 
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7974 \u963 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i they were not; they are not; they shall not be.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 44:24\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Thus says the Lord, who redeems you, who forms you from the womb: I am the Lord, who accomplishes all things; I alone stretched out heaven, and I bolstered 
\f1\i (made firm)
\f2\i0  earth. Who else? \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 44:24, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Observation of supreme importance for our study:
\f2\b0 \
The Lord declares: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u958 \u941 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u957 \u945  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u8056 \u957  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I stretched out the heaven ALONE."
\f2\i0  And 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u941 \u969 \u963 \u945  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u947 \u8134 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I made the earth firm"
\f2\i0  (note the 
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u949 \u972 \u969 
\f2\b0  root \'97 connecting to 
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u941 \u969 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0 , the firmament of Gen 1:6; this will matter when cosmology becomes relevant). And then the challenge: 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u943 \u962  \u7957 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u962 ;
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Who else?"
\f2\i0 \
This single verse forbids any reading of Genesis 1:1 that places a second divine person beside the Father as co-creator. 
\f0\b The Father stretched out the heavens ALONE.
\f2\b0  When we come to examine the Son's role and the meaning of John 1:3 / Col 1:16 / 1 Cor 8:6 ("through Him"), we must reconcile those texts with 
\f0\b this
\f2\b0  declaration \'97 not the other way around. 
\f0\b God speaks first; men interpret after.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 ISAIAH 45 \'97 "I am the Lord, and there is none else"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 45:5-6\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 because I am the Lord God, and there is no other god besides me, and you did not know me, \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 45:5, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf0 so that they who are from the rising of the sun and from its going down may know that there is no one besides me; I am the Lord God, and there is no other. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 45:6, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Observation:
\f2\b0  Five times in two verses the singularity is hammered: 
\f0\b "I am the Lord, and there is none else."
\f2\b0  This is not the language of a tri-personal 
\f1\i (three persons in one being)
\f2\i0  being veiling part of His identity. This is plain, unambiguous, first-person testimony of 
\f0\b one Being, one God
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 45:18\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Thus says the Lord, who made heaven\'97 this is the God who displayed the earth and made it; he himself marked its limits; he did not make it to be empty but to be inhabited: I am, and there is no other. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 45:18, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Observation:
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u8023 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "This is the God"
\f2\i0  \'97 the One who made the heaven, formed the earth, prepared it, created it for habitation. 
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u7956 \u964 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I AM, and there is none else."
\f2\i0 \
Note the 
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 the same self-disclosure formula that runs through Isaiah and which Jesus will later use of Himself (John 8:58). We will mark this and return to it: the question is 
\f1\i how
\f2\i0  the Son can speak with the voice of the One God, when the One God has declared that there is no other.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 45:21-22\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 If they will declare it, let them draw near so that they may know together who made from the beginning these things that are to be heard. Then it was declared to you, I am God, and there is no other besides me; there is no righteous one or savior except me. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 45:21, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Turn to me, and you shall be saved, you who are from the end of the earth! I am God, and there is no other. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 45:22, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

