\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Foundation Established\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 1. 
\f0\b The One God is numerically one Being
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (one in number
\f2\i0  \'97 not a family, not a committee)
\f1\i  \'97 not a council, not a triad 
\f2\i0 (a group of three)
\f1\i , not a multiplicity of persons sharing essence 
\f2\i0 (one shared being)*.\
2. 
\f0\b He created the heavens and the earth ALONE
\f2\b0  (44:24) \'97 this stands as the controlling text for Genesis 1:1.\
3. 
\f0\b He alone is Saviour
\f2\b0  (45:21).\
4. 
\f0\b To Him alone every knee shall bow
\f2\b0  (45:23).\
5. 
\f0\b He is incomparable
\f2\b0  \'97 no being is 
\f1\i like
\f2\i0  Him (46:5, 9).\
This is the God whom Jesus called 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the only true God
\f2\i0  (John 17:3) \'97 and whom Jesus called 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u945  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957  \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i my Father and my God
\f2\i0  (John 20:17).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Father is the One God of Isaiah 44-46.
\f2\b0  This is our foundation. Any study of the Son must be built upon \'97 and reconciled with \'97 this declaration, never against it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A Question Now Properly Framed\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 With this foundation firm, we may now ask the right question \'97 the question that drives the rest of our study:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Who, then, is the Son of this One God? In what sense is He called "the Word," "the Image," "the Firstborn," "the Lord through whom are all things" \'97 without violating the absolute singularity of the Father?
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We now turn to the Old Testament's earliest posits of the Son \'97 the Father's 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u942 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (only-begotten)
\f2\i0  \'97 built strictly upon the foundation we have laid: 
\f0\b the Father is the One God, and there is none beside Him.
\f2\b0 \
We will proceed chronologically as the prophecies are given in the canonical order, beginning at the earliest.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 POSIT #1 \'97 Genesis 3:15: The Seed of the Woman\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And I will put enmity between you and between the woman and between your offspring and between her offspring; he will watch your head, and you will watch his heel." \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 3:15, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Lexham English Septuagint keeps the older English for 
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u960 \u941 \u961 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (seed)
\f2\i0  \'97 and carries the same masculine singular:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 "I will place enmity between you and the woman, and between your seed and her seed; he will watch your head carefully, and you will watch his heel carefully." \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 3:15, LES
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  The pronoun 
\f0\b \uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  is masculine singular \'97 "
\f0\b He
\f2\b0 , He Himself" \'97 not 
\f1\i it
\f2\i0 , not 
\f1\i they
\f2\i0 . The LXX is grammatically remarkable here: the antecedent 
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u960 \u941 \u961 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i seed
\f2\i0 ) is 
\f0\b neuter
\f2\b0 , which would normally demand 
\f0\b \uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 
\f2\b0 . Yet the translators of the LXX (3rd-2nd century BC, 
\f1\i centuries before any Christian influence
\f2\i0 ) deliberately rendered 
\f0\b \uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 masculine \'97 pointing to a singular 
\f0\b male person
\f2\b0  as the Seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 A HISTORICAL NOTE:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i The Greek Old Testament was rendered in the third through second centuries before Christ, for Greek-speaking Jews \'97 long before any Christian influence could have shaped its words.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the first prophetic posit of the coming 
\f0\b One
\f2\b0  \'97 a single human Person, born of a woman, who will crush the head of the serpent 
\f1\i (the Hebrew wording as Geneva renders it; the LXX seat above reads, "he will watch your head")
\f2\i0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (2)
\f2\b0  "
\f0\b The seed of the woman
\f2\b0 " \'97 not of the man. In the entire patriarchal framework of Scripture, seed is reckoned through the father. This phrase is anomalous \'97 it anticipates a birth not according to the line of a human father. The two witnesses for this anomaly being fulfilled:\

\f0\b Isaiah 7:14 (LXX):
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Therefore the Lord himself will give you a sign. Look, the virgin shall be with child and bear a son, and you shall name him Emmanouel 
\f1\i (Immanuel)
\f2\i0 . \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 7:14, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The LXX explicitly says 
\f0\b \uc0\u7969  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the virgin
\f2\i0  \'97 not merely 
