\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Psalm immediately distinguishes 
\f0\b two parties
\f2\b0  on the divine side:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the Lord
\f2\i0  (the Father, the One God of Isaiah 44-46)\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f3\i\b His
\f0\i0  Anointed
\f2\b0  \'97 the Christ who belongs 
\f1\i to
\f2\i0  the Lord\
The Anointed is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  the Lord; He belongs to the Lord. He is the Lord's 
\f1\i Christ
\f2\i0 . The genitive 
\f0\b \uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  ("of Him / His") is decisive \'97 it forbids identifying the Christ as the same Being as the Lord who anoints Him.\
This is the very pattern Peter preaches at Pentecost:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Acts 2:36 (Geneva):
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Therefore, let all the house of Israel know for a surety, that God hath made him both Lord, and Christ, this Jesus, I say, whom ye have crucified. \'97 
\f0\b Acts 2:36, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Peter declares that 
\f0\b God MADE Him
\f2\b0  (
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0 ) both Lord and Christ. The Father \'97 the One God \'97 is the One who 
\f1\i makes
\f2\i0  Jesus Lord and Christ. Jesus is not the One making; He is the One 
\f1\i being made
\f2\i0  into His offices by the Father.\
