\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of the utmost weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u952 \u951 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u8058 \u962  \u8017 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I was established as king BY HIM."
\f2\i0  The Son does not crown Himself; He is 
\f0\b made
\f2\b0  king 
\f0\b by the Father
\f2\b0 . This is again the language of dependence and appointment, not co-equality.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u933 \u7985 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u949 \u7990  \u963 \u973 , \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u963 \u942 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u957  \u947 \u949 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u957 \u951 \u954 \u940  \u963 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "My Son art Thou; I, today, have begotten Thee."
\f2\i0 \
This is the 
\f0\b first explicit declaration in the Psalter
\f2\b0  of the Father-Son relation, and it tells us two crucial things:\

\f0\b (a)
\f2\b0  The Son is 
\f0\b begotten
\f2\b0  (
\f0\b \uc0\u947 \u949 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u957 \u951 \u954 \u945 
\f2\b0 ) \'97 He has an origin in the Father. This is the very meaning of 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u942 \u962 
\f2\b0  (only-begotten) \'97 
\f1\i singularly brought forth from the Father.
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b (b)
\f2\b0  This begetting is fixed to a 
\f0\b day
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u942 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i today
\f2\i0 ) \'97 a definite moment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 When is "today"? \'97 The two witnesses of the Apostles:\
