\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Note on the textual difference\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The LXX reads 
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u961 \u940 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u960 \u945 \u953 \u948 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "lay hold of instruction/discipline"
\f2\i0  \'97 where the Hebrew has 
\f1\i "kiss the Son"
\f2\i0  (the wording of the 1599 Geneva and the English tradition). This is a notable variant. Either reading, the climactic line is the same: 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u945 \u954 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u953  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u959 \u7985  \u960 \u949 \u960 \u959 \u953 \u952 \u972 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 
