\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation \'97 a remarkable inversion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 In v. 1 the Son sits at the Father's right hand. In v. 5 
\f1\i the Lord is at
\f2\i0  
\f0\b the Son's
\f2\b0  
\f1\i right hand
\f2\i0 . This is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  a contradiction; it is the picture of the 
\f0\b Father and the Son operating in perfect coordination
\f2\b0  \'97 wherever the Son acts in judgment, the Father stands with Him; wherever the Father is enthroned, the Son sits at His right.\
The Father and Son are 
\f0\b two distinct figures
\f2\b0 , working together \'97 never collapsed into one Person, never elevated to two Gods. 
\f0\b One God, the Father; one Lord, His Christ \'97 at one another's right hand.
\f2\b0 \
