\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 A doctrinal observation per our maxims\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Notice carefully what Proverbs 8 does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  say:\
- It does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  say Wisdom is co-eternal in the sense of having no beginning. It explicitly says she was 
\f0\b founded / begotten
\f2\b0  by the Lord.\
- It does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  say Wisdom is 
\f1\i another God
\f2\i0 . She is the Lord's Wisdom \'97 belonging to Him, brought forth from Him.\
- It does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  violate Isaiah 44:24. The Lord stretches out the heavens 
\f1\i alone
\f2\i0  \'97 by His own Wisdom, which is His. The Wisdom acting is 
\f1\i His
\f2\i0 , not a separate Deity.\
This perfectly preserves the Shema and Isaiah 44-46 while honestly testifying to the Son's pre-temporal begetting. 
\f0\b The Son has an origin in the Father; the Father has no origin.
\f2\b0  This is the consistent biblical witness, and it is the testimony of the LXX our Lord used.\
