\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Doctrinal Picture \'97 Strictly From Scripture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Son of the One God:\
- 
\f0\b Was brought forth
\f2\b0  by the Father before time and the creation (
\f0\b \uc0\u947 \u949 \u957 \u957 \u8119  \u956 \u949 
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u952 \u949 \u956 \u949 \u955 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 
\f2\b0 ).\
- 
\f0\b Was with the Father
\f2\b0  as His Wisdom at the work of creation (Prov 8; cf. John 1:1 \'97 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0 ).\
- 
\f0\b Came forth
\f2\b0  in the fullness of time, born of the virgin in Bethlehem (Mic 5:2; Gen 3:15; Isa 7:14; Gal 4:4).\
- 
\f0\b Was begotten in power
\f2\b0  as Son of God by the resurrection (Ps 2:7; Rom 1:4; Acts 13:33).\
- 
\f0\b Was seated
\f2\b0  at the Father's right hand, made both Lord and Christ (Ps 110:1; Acts 2:36).\
- 
\f0\b Is Priest forever
\f2\b0  by oath of the Father (Ps 110:4; Heb 7:21).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 At every point, the Father is the Source, the Sender, the Appointer, the Anointer, the Begetter, the Glorifier.
\f2\b0  The Son is the brought-forth, the sent, the appointed, the anointed, the begotten, the glorified \'97 
\f0\b and acts always for the Father's purposes
\f2\b0  (Mic 5:2: 
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i for Me
\f2\i0 ).\
The Shema stands. Isaiah 44-46 stands. 
\f0\b The Father is the One God.
\f2\b0  The Son is His Only-Begotten \'97 distinct, beloved, exalted, but never a second God, never a co-equal, never the Father.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A Question Now Properly Opened\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Micah 5:2 spoke of the Son's 
\f0\b goings-forth
\f2\b0  (plural) 
\f0\b from the beginning
\f2\b0 . We have accounted for:\
- His begetting (Prov 8 / Ps 109:3 LXX).\
- His birth in Bethlehem (Mic 5:2 / Isa 7:14).\
But what of the 
\f0\b intermediate goings-forth
\f2\b0  \'97 His appearances in the Old Testament between His begetting and His birth?\
Scripture testifies to a Person called 
\f0\b the Angel of the LORD
\f2\b0  (
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u7940 \u947 \u947 \u949 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 literally, 
\f1\i the Messenger of the LORD
\f2\i0 ) who appears repeatedly \'97 to Hagar, Abraham, Jacob, Moses, Gideon, Manoah \'97 and who 
\f1\i speaks as God
\f2\i0 , is 
\f1\i worshipped
\f2\i0 , yet is 
\f1\i sent from God
\f2\i0 . Is this Person the pre-incarnate Son \'97 one of the 
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u958 \u959 \u948 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  of Micah 5:2?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A QUESTION ARISING \'97 Who Is the Angel of the LORD?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 One of the most consequential threads in all of Scripture now opens \'97 the appearances of 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u7940 \u947 \u947 \u949 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i the Messenger of the LORD
\f2\i0 ). The texts must establish, by two-or-more witnesses, whether this Messenger is: (a) merely a created angel acting as God's spokesman, or (b) the One God Himself appearing, or (c) a distinct Person who speaks 
\f1\i as
\f2\i0  God yet is 
\f1\i sent by
\f2\i0  God \'97 i.e., the pre-incarnate Son in one of His 
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u958 \u959 \u948 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (the goings-forth)
\f2\i0  (Micah 5:2).\
Per our maxims, we will not impose the answer; we will let Scripture deliver it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE FIRST APPEARANCE \'97 Genesis 16: Hagar in the Wilderness\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 But the Lord God's angel found her by the spring of water in the wilderness, by the spring on the way to Sour 
\f1\i (Shur)
\f2\i0 . And the angel of the Lord said to her, "Hagar, slave-girl of Sara 
\f1\i (Sarai)
\f2\i0 , where are you coming from, and where are you going?" \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 16:7-8, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The angel of the Lord also said to her, "I will multitudinously 
\f1\i (greatly)
\f2\i0  multiply your offspring, and it will not be counted for multitude." \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 16:10, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of decisive importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Messenger says: 
\f0\b "I will multiply your seed."
\f2\b0  This is a promise that 
\f0\b only God can make and fulfill
\f2\b0  \'97 and it is the 
\f0\b same promise
\f2\b0  the LORD Himself makes directly to Abraham (Gen 13:16; 15:5; 22:17). The Messenger does not say 
\f1\i "The LORD will multiply"
\f2\i0 ; He says 
\f0\b "I will multiply."
\f2\b0  He speaks in the first person 
\f1\i as God
\f2\i0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And Hagar called the name of the Lord who was speaking to her, "You-are-the-God-who-looksupon-me 
\f1\i (You are the God who sees me)
\f2\i0 ," because she said, "For truly I saw him face to face when he appeared to me." \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 16:13, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of the utmost weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Hagar identifies the Messenger as 
\f0\b \uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the LORD
\f2\i0  \'97 and addresses Him as 
\f0\b \uc0\u931 \u8058  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "You are the God."
\f2\i0  Furthermore, she marvels that she has 
\f0\b seen
\f2\b0  Him and lived: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957 \u974 \u960 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u949 \u7990 \u948 \u959 \u957  \u8000 \u966 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u956 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I have seen face-to-face the One who appeared to me."
\f2\i0 \
The narrator (Moses, by inspiration) does 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  correct her. Scripture 
\f1\i confirms
\f2\i0  her identification: 
\f0\b "she called the name of the LORD who spoke to her: You are the God who sees me."
\f2\b0 \
So here is our first datum: 
\f0\b The Messenger speaks as God, is identified as God, and is seen \'97 yet remains called "the Messenger of the LORD," not the LORD without qualification.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE SECOND APPEARANCE \'97 Genesis 22: The Akedah\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And the Lord's angel called him from the sky 
\f1\i (heaven)
\f2\i0  and said to him, "Abraam 
\f1\i (Abraham)
\f2\i0 , Abraam!" And he said, "Here I am." And he said, "Do not lay your hand on the youngster 
\f1\i (the boy)
\f2\i0  nor do anything to him. For now I know that you do fear God, and for my sake you have not spared your beloved son." \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 22:11-12, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Messenger says: 
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7952 \u966 \u949 \u943 \u963 \u969  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u965 \u7985 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u953 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u941 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "you did not spare your beloved son 
\f3\b for My sake
\f1\b0 ."
\f2\i0 \
But the entire test had been at the command of 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  (v. 1): 
\f1\i "God tested Abraham."
\f2\i0  So the One who is testing \'97 God \'97 is the same One 
\f0\b for whose sake
\f2\b0  Abraham did not spare his son. The Messenger speaks as 
\f0\b the God
\f2\b0  who commanded the test.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And the Lord's angel called Abraam 
\f1\i (Abraham)
\f2\i0  a second time from the sky 
\f1\i (heaven)
\f2\i0 , saying, "By myself I have sworn, says the Lord: Inasmuch as you have carried out this matter and for my sake have not spared your beloved son, I will indeed bless you with blessings, and I will make your offspring as numerously numerous 
\f1\i (greatly multiplied)
\f2\i0  as the stars of the sky and as the sand that is by the seashore, \'85" \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 22:15-18, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of decisive weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Messenger says: 
\f0\b "\uc0\u922 \u945 \u964 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8036 \u956 \u959 \u963 \u945 , \u955 \u941 \u947 \u949 \u953  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 "
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "BY MYSELF I have sworn, says the LORD."
\f2\i0 \
This is identical to Isaiah 45:23 LXX: 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8000 \u956 \u957 \u973 \u969 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "By Myself I swear,"
\f2\i0  which we examined as the Father's exclusive self-oath. The Messenger speaks 
\f0\b as YHWH
\f2\b0  swearing by Himself. He is not merely conveying a message \'97 He is the One swearing, in the first person.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Yet observe carefully
\f2\b0  \'97 the Messenger speaks 
\f0\b as YHWH swearing
\f2\b0 , and yet the formula 
\f0\b \uc0\u955 \u941 \u947 \u949 \u953  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i ("says the LORD")
\f2\i0  is used. This is the prophetic formula \'97 the Messenger speaks for the LORD and as the LORD simultaneously. He is 
\f1\i of
\f2\i0  the LORD and yet speaks 
\f1\i as
\f2\i0  the LORD.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Apostolic confirmation \'97 Hebrews 6:13-14\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 For when God made the promise to Abraham, because he had no greater to swear by, he sware by himself, Saying, Surely I will abundantly bless thee and multiply thee marvelously. \'97 
\f0\b Hebrews 6:13-14, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The author of Hebrews identifies the swearer as 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  Himself. Therefore the 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u947 \u947 \u949 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  of Genesis 22 was speaking 
\f1\i as
\f2\i0  God Himself swearing \'97 yet without being called the LORD without qualification.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE THIRD APPEARANCE \'97 Genesis 31: Jacob and the God of Bethel\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And the angel of God said to me during sleep, \'91Iakob 
\f1\i (Jacob)
\f2\i0 .\'92 And I said, \'91What is it?\'92 \'85 I am the God who appeared to you at a divine place 
\f1\i (the place of God, Bethel)
\f2\i0 , there where you anointed a stele 
\f1\i (pillar)
\f2\i0  to me and made a vow to me there. \'85 \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 31:11-13, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of supreme importance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Messenger says plainly: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I AM the God"
\f2\i0  \'97 the very 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953 
\f2\b0  formula of Isaiah 45:18! He claims to be 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u8001  \u8000 \u966 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the God who appeared to you"
\f2\i0  at Bethel \'97 referring back to Genesis 28 where Jacob saw the ladder and 
\f0\b YHWH
\f2\b0  stood above it.\
So the same Person who appeared to Jacob as 
\f0\b YHWH
\f2\b0  at Bethel now appears as 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u7940 \u947 \u947 \u949 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the Messenger of God.
\f2\i0  He is both: 
\f0\b the appearing God
\f2\b0 , and 
\f0\b the sent Messenger
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE FOURTH APPEARANCE \'97 Genesis 32: Wrestling at Peniel\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And Iakob 
\f1\i (Jacob)
\f2\i0  was left alone, and a man was wrestling with him until morning. \'85 Then he said to him, \'93Your name shall no longer be called Iakob 
\f1\i (Jacob)
\f2\i0 , but Israel shall be your name, because you have prevailed with a god, and with humans you are powerful.\'94 \'85 And Iakob 
\f1\i (Jacob)
\f2\i0  called the name of that place Divine-form 
\f1\i (Peniel, \'93the face of God\'94)
\f2\i0 , \'93For I have seen a god face to face, and my life has been preserved.\'94 \'97 
\f0\b Genesis 32:24-30, LXX (NETS; the Greek editions number these verses 25-31)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of the highest weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The One who wrestles is called 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i a man.
\f2\i0  He is 
\f0\b physically embodied
\f2\b0 , wrestling all night. Yet:\
- He has authority to 
\f0\b rename
\f2\b0  Jacob to 
\f0\b Israel
\f2\b0  (only God renames covenant figures).\
- He declares Jacob has 
\f0\b striven with God
\f2\b0  (
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u949 \u964 \u8048  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0 ).\
- Jacob identifies Him as 
\f0\b \uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I have seen God face to face."
\f2\i0 \
Yet this God is in the form of a 
\f0\b Man
\f2\b0 . Here is a pre-incarnate visible manifestation of a Person who is both 
\f1\i with God
\f2\i0  (whom Jacob strove with) and 
\f1\i appears as Man
\f2\i0  \'97 a foreshadowing of the Incarnation itself.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Prophet Hosea confirms \'97 Hosea 12:3-4 (LXX 12:4-5):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 In the womb he kicked his brother with the heel and in his struggles prevailed against God. And he prevailed with an angel and predominated 
\f1\i (prevailed, overpowered)
\f2\i0  \'85 \'97 
\f0\b Hosea 12:3-4, LXX (NETS; the Greek editions number these verses 4-5)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Prophet's testimony is the second witness:
\f2\b0  In one breath, Jacob's adversary is called 
\f0\b \uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (God)
\f2\i0  and 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u947 \u947 \u949 \u955 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (Angel/Messenger).
\f2\i0  
\f0\b Hosea, under inspiration, identifies the Messenger as God.
\f2\b0  The two designations refer to the same Person.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE FIFTH APPEARANCE \'97 Exodus 3: The Burning Bush\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Now an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a fire of flame out of the bush, \'85 Now when the Lord saw that he was drawing near to see, the Lord called him from the bush, saying, \'93Moyses 
\f1\i (Moses)
\f2\i0 , Moyses.\'94 And he said, \'93What is it?\'94 \'85 And he said to him, \'93I am the God of your father, God of Abraam 
\f1\i (Abraham)
\f2\i0  and God of Isaak 
\f1\i (Isaac)
\f2\i0  and God of Iakob 
\f1\i (Jacob)
\f2\i0 .\'94 \'85 \'97 
\f0\b Exodus 3:2-6, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of the highest order\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The text moves seamlessly between three designations:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u947 \u947 \u949 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (the Messenger of the LORD)
\f2\i0  \'97 v. 2\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (the LORD)
\f2\i0  \'97 v. 4\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  
\f1\i (God)
\f2\i0  \'97 v. 4, 6\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Messenger, the LORD, and God are presented as one and the same speaker
\f2\b0  \'97 yet the text begins by calling Him "the Messenger of the LORD," not "the LORD" simpliciter. Once again: 
\f0\b He speaks as God, is identified as God, yet is named the Messenger sent by God.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Exodus 3:14 (LXX) \'97 The "I AM" Declaration:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And God said to Moyses 
\f1\i (Moses)
\f2\i0 , \'93I am The One Who Is.\'94 And he said, \'93Thus shall you say to the sons of Israel, \'91The One Who Is has sent me to you.\'92\'94 \'97 
\f0\b Exodus 3:14, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Messenger declares Himself: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u8001  \u8036 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "I AM the One Who Is."
\f2\i0  This is the divine Name itself.\
Now hear Jesus, in the New Testament, in John 8:58 (Greek):\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i \cf0 "\uc0\u949 \u7990 \u960 \u949 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962 \'b7 \u7944 \u956 \u8052 \u957  \u7936 \u956 \u8052 \u957  \u955 \u941 \u947 \u969  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 , \u960 \u961 \u8054 \u957  \u7944 \u946 \u961 \u945 \u8048 \u956  \u947 \u949 \u957 \u941 \u963 \u952 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u943 ."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Jesus said unto them, Verily, verily I say unto you, before Abraham was, I am. \'97 
\f0\b John 8:58, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Jews understood this and sought to stone Him for blasphemy. 
\f0\b Jesus claims the very designation the Messenger spoke at the burning bush.
\f2\b0  This is a strong witness \'97 though not yet decisive \'97 that the Messenger of the LORD is the same Person who later was named Jesus.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 THE APOSTOLIC IDENTIFICATION \'97 Two Decisive Witnesses\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We have seen the pattern \'97 the Messenger speaks as God, is called God, is seen as God, yet is sent by God and remains "the Messenger." Who, then, is He? The Apostles, by inspiration, supply the answer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Witness #1 \'97 1 Corinthians 10:1-4, 9:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Moreover, brethren, I would not that ye should be ignorant, that all our fathers were under that cloud, and all passed through that sea, \'85 And did all drink the same spiritual drink (for they drank of the spiritual Rock that followed them: and the Rock was Christ) \'85 Neither let us tempt Christ, as some of them also tempted him, and were destroyed of serpents. \'97 
\f0\b 1 Corinthians 10:1-4, 9, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Paul declares that the One who led Israel through the wilderness \'97 the One they tempted, the Rock that gave them water (which the Old Testament names as 
\f2\b0 YHWH
\f0\b ) \'97 was Christ.
\f2\b0  This is Paul's unambiguous identification of the One who appeared, spoke, led, and acted in the Exodus narrative as 
\f0\b the pre-incarnate Christ
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Witness #2 \'97 Jude 5:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 I will therefore put you in remembrance, forasmuch as ye once knew this, how that 
\f1\i (that)
\f2\i0  the Lord, after that he had delivered the people out of Egypt, destroyed them afterward which believed not 
\f1\i (those who did not believe)
\f2\i0 . \'97 
\f0\b Jude 5, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Note:
\f2\b0  The earliest and best-attested reading is 
\f0\b \uc0\u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Jesus saved a people out of Egypt."
\f2\i0  Jude, by inspiration, identifies the 
\f0\b Deliverer of Israel from Egypt
\f2\b0  \'97 who in Exodus is called 
\f0\b YHWH
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b the Messenger of the LORD
\f2\b0  \'97 as 
\f0\b Jesus
\f2\b0 . Even taking the Geneva's variant "the Lord," the witness still holds, since Paul has already established (1 Cor 10) that "the Lord" of the wilderness is Christ.\

\f0\b Two witnesses established:
\f2\b0  The Messenger of the LORD \'97 the One who appeared to Hagar, swore the oath to Abraham, wrestled with Jacob, spoke from the burning bush, led Israel through the sea, gave the water from the Rock \'97 is 
\f0\b the pre-incarnate Christ, the Son of the One God
\f2\b0 , in one of His 
\f0\b \uc0\u7956 \u958 \u959 \u948 \u959 \u953 
\f2\b0  (Mic 5:2).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 HOW IS THIS CONSISTENT WITH OUR FOUNDATION? \'97 A Critical Reconciliation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Per our maxims, we must reconcile this finding with Isaiah 44-46 and the absolute monotheism of the Shema. 
\f0\b How can the Son be "seen as God" when the Father said, "No man can see Me and live" (Ex 33:20) and "To whom will you liken Me?" (Isa 46:5)?
\f2\b0 \
The answer is given by Jesus Himself and confirmed by John:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 John 1:18:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 No man hath seen God at any time: that only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared 
\f1\i (revealed)
\f2\i0  him. \'97 
\f0\b John 1:18, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 John 6:46:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Not that any man hath seen the Father, save 
\f1\i (except)
\f2\i0  he which is of God, he hath seen the Father. \'97 
\f0\b John 6:46, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The reconciliation, by Scripture itself:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - 
\f0\b No man has ever seen the Father.
\f2\b0  Hagar did not see the Father. Abraham did not see the Father. Jacob did not see the Father. Moses did not see the Father. 
\f1\i Period.
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b The One whom they all saw \'97 and called "God" \'97 was the Only-Begotten Son
\f2\b0 , the visible Image (
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u954 \u8060 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u959 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0 , Col 1:15) of the invisible Father.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Therefore Isaiah 44-46 is not violated.
\f2\b0  The Father remains unseen, unique, the sole God. The Son is the visible Messenger of that God \'97 His Begotten, sent forth from the Father from of old, bearing the Father's authority, Name, and message.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A Crucial Textual Note: Exodus 23:20-21\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Exodus 23:20-21, LXX (NETS):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And look, I am sending my angel in front of you in order to guard you on the way in order to bring you into the land that I prepared for you. Mind yourself 
\f1\i (take care)
\f2\i0 , and listen to him, and do not disobey him. For he shall not hold you in undue awe 
\f1\i (he will not spare you)
\f2\i0 , for my name is upon him. \'97 
\f0\b Exodus 23:20-21, LXX (NETS)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Father says of this Messenger: 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u940  \u956 \u959 \u973  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "My Name is in Him."
\f2\i0  This is the Father's own explanation for why this Messenger speaks as God, acts as God, must be obeyed as God, and forgives or refuses to forgive sins \'97 because 
\f0\b the Father's Name dwells in Him.
\f2\b0 \
Geneva 
\f1\i (1599)
\f2\i0  prints the same clause of the Angel at verse 21: \'93for he will not spare your misdeeds, because my Name is in him.\'94 (NETS reads \'93my name is upon him\'94; the Greek \uc0\u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  carries either rendering.)\
This is the very same theme Jesus declared in His high-priestly prayer:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 John 17:11-12:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And now am I no more in the world, but these are in the world, and I come to thee. Holy Father, keep them in thy Name, even them whom thou hast given me, that they may be one, as we are. While I was with them in the world, I kept them in thy Name: those that thou gavest me, have I kept, and none of them is lost, but the child of perdition, that the Scripture might be fulfilled. \'97 
\f0\b John 17:11-12, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Name of the Father was given to the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 exactly as it was placed in the Messenger at Exodus 23:21. This is the 
\f0\b same Person
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
