\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What Remains Standing About the Son's Pre-Temporal Existence\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 If we strip out the inferences from Proverbs 8, what direct OT-and-NT-witnessed evidence do we have for the Son existing 
\f0\b before
\f2\b0  His birth in Bethlehem?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Psalm 109:3 LXX
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "From the womb, before the morning star, I have begotten Thee."
\f2\i0  This is spoken by the Father to the One Psalm 110:1 distinguishes from Him. The NT cites Psalm 110 extensively in reference to the Son, though the specific phrase "before the morning star" is not, to my recollection, explicitly quoted in the NT.\

\f0\b Micah 5:2
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "whose goings-forth are from the beginning, from days of old/eternity."
\f2\i0  The NT (Matthew 2:5-6) cites Micah 5:2 in reference to the birthplace, but does not explicitly quote the "goings-forth" phrase. So the "goings-forth from of old" is in the OT text but is not specifically expounded in the NT.\

\f0\b Therefore even the Son's pre-temporal existence
\f2\b0  \'97 which I had treated as firmly established \'97 rests on 
\f0\b less explicit NT confirmation
\f2\b0  than I had presented. The OT phrases are 
\f1\i there
\f2\i0  in the LXX text the Apostles used, but their explicit handling of those specific phrases is sparse.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Going Forward\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 I owe you greater discipline. Let me set a stricter standard for the remainder of our study:\
1. I will distinguish 
\f0\b what the text strictly says
\f2\b0  from 
\f0\b what is suggested by parallel
\f2\b0 .\
2. I will not assert an identification as "established by two witnesses" unless the NT or another OT text 
\f0\b explicitly handles the same passage
\f2\b0  or makes an unambiguous identification.\
3. Where parallels exist but no explicit witness binds them, I will say so plainly: 
\f1\i "This is a suggestive parallel; it is not a witnessed identification."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

