\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 The Refined Foundation Standing After Audit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 What we have securely, with strict witness-establishment, is this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 1. There is one God: the Father.
\f2\b0  (Multiple direct witnesses, both OT and from Jesus' own lips.)\

\f0\b 2. There is one Lord: Jesus Christ \'97 the Father's Anointed Son.
\f2\b0  This is established by:\
- 
\f0\b Psalm 2
\f2\b0  explicitly cited as fulfilled in Jesus (Acts 4, 13; Heb 1, 5).\
- 
\f0\b Psalm 110
\f2\b0  explicitly cited as fulfilled in Jesus (Matt 22; Acts 2; Heb 1, 5, 7).\
- 
\f0\b Micah 5:2 (Bethlehem)
\f2\b0  explicitly cited as fulfilled in Jesus (Matt 2).\

\f0\b 3. The Son was begotten / made / declared Son of God in power by His resurrection.
\f2\b0  Explicitly:\
- 
\f0\b Acts 13:33
\f2\b0  \'97 Paul applies Psalm 2:7 to the resurrection: 
\f1\i Geneva: "in that he raised up Jesus, even as it is written in the second Psalm, Thou art my Son: this day have I begotten thee."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Rom 1:4
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i Geneva: "declared mightily to be the Son of God ... by the resurrection from the dead"
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Acts 2:36
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i Geneva: "God hath made him both Lord, and Christ, this Jesus, I say, whom ye have crucified"
\f2\i0  \'97 at His exaltation.\

\f0\b 4. The Son is at the Father's right hand, made both Lord and Christ by the Father, and is forever Priest by the Father's oath.
\f2\b0  (Ps 110:1, 4; Acts 2:36; Heb 7:21)\

\f0\b 5. Genesis 22 is a typological figure of the Father offering His beloved Son.
\f2\b0  (Heb 11:17-19)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What we do NOT have firmly established by explicit witness:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - That the Son existed personally before His conception in Mary.\
- That the Son was the agent of original creation (Gen 1).\
- That the Son is the personified Wisdom of Proverbs 8.\
- That the Son is the Angel/Messenger of the LORD.\
These are claims that have been made for centuries \'97 by patristic writers, by creeds, by tradition \'97 but the 
\f0\b strict two-witness establishment from explicit Scripture is not as firm as I had presented
\f2\b0 . They are 
\f1\i possible
\f2\i0 . They may even be probable. But they are not established with the certainty I had implied.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

