\f0\b What "\uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 " means:
\f2\b0  This is the critical lexical question. 
\f0\b \uc0\u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  in Greek can mean:\
- A spoken word, utterance, declaration\
- A reasoned account, message, report\
- A principle, plan, rational expression\
- (In some philosophical usage) a personified rational principle\

\f0\b John does not define the term in v. 1.
\f2\b0  He uses it without explanation, as if his readers should know. We must ask: 
\f1\i does Scripture itself establish what John means by
\f2\i0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0 ?\
