\f0\b \cf0 What the text strictly says:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "with/toward God."
\f2\i0  The preposition 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u961 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  with the accusative often indicates orientation, presence-toward, face-to-face relation.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the God"
\f2\i0  \'97 definite article. Per our foundation, 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  in NT usage virtually always refers to 
\f0\b the Father
\f2\b0  (see John 17:3; 1 Cor 8:6).\

\f0\b Honest observation:
\f2\b0  The Word is 
\f0\b with
\f2\b0  the God (the Father). This phrase distinguishes 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  from 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0 . The Word is 
\f1\i toward / with
\f2\i0  God \'97 implying relation, not identity-of-person.\
