This is a significant statement. John the Baptist was 
\f0\b born before
\f2\b0  Jesus (six months earlier, per Luke 1:36). Yet John says Jesus 
\f0\b was prior
\f2\b0  to him (
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u7974 \u957 
\f2\b0 ). The natural reading: John is testifying to a 
\f1\i priority of being
\f2\i0  of the One coming after him in time \'97 i.e., a pre-existence of some kind.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 However
\f2\b0 , the word 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  can also mean 
\f1\i "of higher rank"
\f2\i0  or 
\f1\i "chief"
\f2\i0  \'97 and this is its meaning in some contexts. The Geneva captures this by translating: 
\f1\i "for he was better than I."
\f2\i0  This rendering preserves the ambiguity \'97 John may be testifying to 
\f1\i priority of being
\f2\i0  or to 
\f1\i priority of rank
\f2\i0 .\

\f0\b Honest assessment:
\f2\b0  v. 15 admits both readings.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Verse 16-17\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \uc0\u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u960 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u7952 \u955 \u940 \u946 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "of His fullness we all received."
\f2\i0  The Word/Son has fullness; we receive from it. This is consistent with Acts 2:33: Jesus, exalted, 
\f1\i received
\f2\i0  the promise of the Spirit from the Father and 
\f1\i poured it out
\f2\i0  on the disciples. The fullness comes from the Father through the Son to us.\

\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u924 \u969 \u971 \u963 \u941 \u969 \u962  \u7952 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951 , \u7969  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7969  \u7936 \u955 \u942 \u952 \u949 \u953 \u945  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u959 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Law was given through Moses; grace and truth came through Jesus Christ."
\f2\i0  Now Jesus is named explicitly. The Word-become-flesh is 
\f0\b Jesus Christ
\f2\b0 . John has fully identified His subject.\
