\f0\b The Father created all things 
\f3\i through
\f0\i0  the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 the Son as agent, the Father as source (1 Cor 8:6; Col 1:16; Heb 1:2; John 1:3).\
4. 
\f0\b The Son emptied Himself, became flesh, and was obedient unto death
\f2\b0  (John 1:14; Phil 2:7-8).\
5. 
\f0\b The Father exalted Him, made Him Lord and Christ, and gave Him the Name above every name
\f2\b0  \'97 at His resurrection and ascension (Acts 2:36; 13:33; Phil 2:9-11; Rom 1:4).\
6. 
\f0\b The Son is at the Father's right hand, Priest forever, ruling until His enemies are made His footstool
\f2\b0  (Ps 110; Acts 2:34; Heb 5-7).\
7. 
\f0\b At every point, the Father is the Source, the Sender, the Appointer, the Glorifier \'97 and the Son is the Sent One, the One who acts for the Father's will and glory.
