\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Psalm 21:16 LXX (22:16 MT) \'97 The Piercing of Hands and Feet\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 because many dogs encircled me, a gathering of evildoers surrounded me. They gouged my hands and feet; \'97 
\f0\b Psalm 21:16 LXX (22:16 MT), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8036 \u961 \u965 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u967 \u949 \u8150 \u961 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u972 \u948 \u945 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "they pierced/dug my hands and feet."
\f2\i0  The verb 
\f0\b \uc0\u8000 \u961 \u973 \u963 \u963 \u969 
\f2\b0  means to dig, to pierce, to bore through. The LXX rendering is unambiguous: hands and feet are 
\f0\b pierced
\f2\b0 .\

\f0\b (2) This is a remarkable witness.
\f2\b0  The LXX was translated centuries before crucifixion was known as a Jewish or Christian theme. The reading "they pierced my hands and feet" is in the 
\f0\b pre-Christian Greek text
\f2\b0 . The Masoretic Hebrew has a contested reading (\uc0\u1499 \u1464 \u1468 \u1488 \u1458 \u1512 \u1460 \u1497  \'97 
\f1\i "like a lion"
\f2\i0  vs. \uc0\u1499 \u1464 \u1468 \u1488 \u1458 \u1512 \u1493 \u1468  \'97 
\f1\i "they pierced"
\f2\i0 ) that has been used by some to obscure the prophecy. The LXX preserves the unambiguous prophetic reading. 
\f0\b Per our maxim #1, we let God be true
\f2\b0  \'97 and the God-breathed text Jesus and the Apostles used reads 
\f0\b \uc0\u8036 \u961 \u965 \u958 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witnesses \'97 the fulfillment:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Behold mine hands and my feet: for it is I myself: handle me, and see: for a spirit hath not flesh and bones, as ye see me have. And when he had thus spoken, he showed them his hands and feet. \'97 
\f0\b Luke 24:39-40, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
Except I see in his hands the print of the nails ... I will not believe ... he said to Thomas, Put thy finger here, and see mine hands, and put forth thine hand, and put it into my side \'97 
\f0\b John 20:25-27, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The risen Jesus shows His 
\f0\b pierced hands and feet
\f2\b0  \'97 fulfilling Ps 21:16 LXX exactly. Two NT witnesses (Luke and John) record the same proof.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Psalm 21:18 LXX (22:18 MT) \'97 Garments Divided and Lots Cast\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 they divided my clothes among themselves, and for my clothing they cast lots. \'97 
\f0\b Psalm 21:18 LXX (22:18 MT), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 the most explicit citation in the NT:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Then the soldiers when they had crucified Jesus, took his garments, (and made four parts, to every soldier a part) and his coat: and the coat was without seam, woven from the top throughout. Therefore they said one to another, Let us not divide it, but cast lots for it, whose it shall be. This was that the Scripture might be fulfilled, which saith, They parted my garments among them, and on my coat did cast lots. So the souldiers did these things in deede. \'97 
\f0\b John 19:23-24, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 John quotes Psalm 21:18 LXX 
\f0\b verbatim
\f2\b0  as the fulfilled Scripture. This is one of the most precise prophecy-fulfillment correspondences in all of Scripture: the 
\f1\i exact
\f2\i0  manner of dividing garments and casting lots is foretold and historically fulfilled.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 This is also recorded by all four Gospels
\f2\b0  \'97 Matthew 27:35, Mark 15:24, Luke 23:34, John 19:23-24 \'97 making it a quadruple witness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

