\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 I will tell of your name to my kindred; in the midst of an assembly I will sing a hymn to you: \'97 
\f0\b Psalm 21:22 LXX (22:22 MT), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 explicit NT citation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 For he that sanctifieth, and they which are sanctified, are all of one: wherefore he is not ashamed to call them brethren, Saying, I will declare thy Name unto my brethren: in the midst of the Church will I sing praises to thee. \'97 
\f0\b Hebrews 2:11-12, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The author of Hebrews 
\f0\b explicitly cites Psalm 22:22 as words spoken by the Christ to the Father
\f2\b0 . This is decisive: 
\f0\b the entire Psalm is the voice of the Christ
\f2\b0 , and the resurrected Son declares the Father's Name to His brethren in the midst of the Church. The Psalm moves from forsakenness (v. 1) to vindication and proclamation (v. 22) \'97 i.e., 
\f0\b death and resurrection
\f2\b0  are the arc of the Psalm.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

