\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Isaiah 52:13-15 LXX \'97 The Servant's Exaltation and Disfigurement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 See, my servant shall understand, and he shall be exalted and glorified exceedingly. Just as many shall be astonished at you\'97 so shall your appearance be without glory from men, and your glory be absent from the men\'97 so shall many nations be astonished at him, and kings shall shut their mouth, because those who were not informed about him shall see and those who did not hear shall understand. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 52:13-15 LXX, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u960 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "My Servant"
\f2\i0  (or 
\f1\i "My Child"
\f2\i0 ). The LXX uses 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u8150 \u962 
\f2\b0 , which can mean both "servant" and "child/son." This same word is used of Jesus in the apostolic preaching:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 For doubtless against thine holy Son Jesus, whom thou hadst anointed, both Herod and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles and the people of Israel gathered themselves together. \'97 
\f0\b Acts 4:27, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Acts 3:13, 26 \'97 same designation of Jesus as 
\f2\b0 \uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u8150 \u948 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u957 
\f0\b  \'97 "His Servant/Child Jesus."
\f2\b0 \
This is the apostolic identification: 
\f0\b Jesus is the \uc0\u960 \u945 \u8150 \u962  of Isaiah 52-53.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8017 \u968 \u969 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u948 \u959 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u963 \u966 \u972 \u948 \u961 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He shall be exalted and glorified exceedingly."
\f2\i0  The Servant's path is exaltation. This corresponds to 
\f0\b John 12:32
\f2\b0 : 
\f1\i "And I, if I be lifted up, will draw all unto Me."
\f2\i0  John explicitly connects Jesus' "being lifted up" to His glorification (John 12:23, 32; 13:31-32).\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7936 \u948 \u959 \u958 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u949 \u7990 \u948 \u972 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Your appearance shall be without glory from men."
\f2\i0  The Servant is 
\f1\i disfigured
\f2\i0  \'97 His visible form unrecognizable. This is fulfilled in Jesus' scourging, beating, and crucifixion.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u952 \u945 \u965 \u956 \u940 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7956 \u952 \u957 \u951  \u960 \u959 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Many nations shall marvel at Him."
\f2\i0  The nations are again in view (cf. Gen 49:10; Ps 21:27-28). The Servant is for the nations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 explicit NT citation of Isa 52:15:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 ... But as it is written, To whom he was not spoken of, they shall see him, and they that heard not, shall understand him. \'97 
\f0\b Romans 15:20-21, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Paul 
\f0\b explicitly cites Isa 52:15 LXX
\f2\b0  as fulfilled in his Gospel preaching to the nations. The Servant is Christ; the nations are the Gentiles.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
