\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1) Multiple explicit NT citations
\f2\b0  of Isa 53:4-6 applied directly to Jesus' atoning work.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b Peter's citation in 1 Pet 2:24-25 binds together vv. 4, 5, 6 of Isa 53.
\f2\b0  This is one of the most explicit and theologically loaded apostolic uses of the OT. The Servant's stripes heal 
\f1\i us
\f2\i0 ; the Servant bears 
\f1\i our
\f2\i0  sins on the 
\f1\i tree
\f2\i0  (\uc0\u958 \u973 \u955 \u959 \u957  \'97 cross).\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  The phrase 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u949 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u964 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u953 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "and the LORD delivered Him over for our sins"
\f2\i0  \'97 is significant. 
\f0\b The Father delivers up the Son
\f2\b0  for our sins. This is the language Paul echoes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Who spared not his own Son, but gave him for us all \'97 
\f0\b Romans 8:32, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
Who was delivered to death for our sins \'97 
\f0\b Romans 4:25, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

