\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u946 \u959 \u973 \u955 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u960 \u955 \u951 \u947 \u8134 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "The LORD wills/desires to cleanse Him from the stroke."
\f2\i0  The Father's purpose is in the Servant's suffering \'97 yet also in His vindication.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u8048 \u957  \u948 \u8182 \u964 \u949  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 , \u7969  \u968 \u965 \u967 \u8052  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8004 \u968 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u963 \u960 \u941 \u961 \u956 \u945  \u956 \u945 \u954 \u961 \u972 \u946 \u953 \u959 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "If you give for sin, your soul shall see long-living seed."
\f2\i0  The Servant's life becomes a sin-offering (
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 the technical term for the sin-offering in Levitical law). His 
\f0\b seed
\f2\b0  survives Him \'97 this is 
\f0\b resurrection language
\f2\b0 .\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u949 \u8150 \u958 \u945 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u966 \u8182 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to show Him light."
\f2\i0  After His soul's labor, He sees 
\f0\b light
\f2\b0 . This is 
\f0\b resurrection
\f2\b0  \'97 the Servant who was cut off from the land of the living (v. 8) now sees light.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u8182 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u948 \u943 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u949 \u8022  \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u960 \u959 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u8150 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "to justify the Righteous One serving many well."
\f2\i0  The Servant is 
\f0\b the Righteous One
\f2\b0  who 
\f0\b justifies many
\f2\b0 .\
