\cf0 # 
\f0\b SYNTHESIS \'97 What is Established by the Whole Counsel
\f2\b0 \
By the most extensive and explicit OT-NT correspondence in Scripture, the following is established with overwhelming witness:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Suffering, Death, Burial, and Vindication of the Son\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 1. 
\f0\b The Son is the prophesied Servant of the LORD
\f2\b0  \'97 identified explicitly by the Apostles (Acts 3:13, 26; 4:27, 30; 8:32-35), by Jesus Himself (Luke 22:37), and by the Father's voice at the baptism (using Isa 42:1 language).\
2. 
\f0\b He was forsaken by the Father on the cross
\f2\b0 , bearing the cry of Psalm 22:1 (Matt 27:46; Mark 15:34).\
3. 
\f0\b He was pierced in His hands and feet
\f2\b0 , with garments divided and lots cast (Ps 22:16, 18; all four Gospels; John 19:23-24 explicit).\
4. 
\f0\b He was silent before His accusers
\f2\b0  as a lamb led to slaughter (Isa 53:7; Acts 8:32; Matt 27:12-14).\
5. 
\f0\b He bore the sins of many
\f2\b0  \'97 making His soul a sin-offering (Isa 53:6, 10-12; 1 Pet 2:24; Rom 4:25; 8:32; Heb 9:28).\
6. 
\f0\b He was cut off from the land of the living
\f2\b0  \'97 He really died (Isa 53:8).\
7. 
\f0\b He was buried with the rich
\f2\b0  (Isa 53:9; Matt 27:57-60).\
8. 
\f0\b He was vindicated, seeing light and seed after His soul's travail
\f2\b0  \'97 He rose from the dead (Isa 53:10-11; Acts 13:33 \'97 
\f1\i "today have I begotten Thee"
\f2\i0  fulfilled in resurrection).\
9. 
\f0\b He justifies many by His righteousness
\f2\b0  (Isa 53:11; Rom 5:18-19).\
10. 
\f0\b The nations have heard and seen what was not previously declared
\f2\b0  \'97 the Gospel goes to the Gentiles (Isa 52:15; Rom 15:21).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A Critical Theological Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Notice carefully what these prophecies establish \'97 and what they do 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  establish.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What they establish:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - The Son's true humanity (a Man, with form, with thirst, with sorrow, with death).\
- The Son's true suffering (forsakenness, piercing, silence, death).\
- The Son's substitutionary work (He bore 
\f1\i our
\f2\i0  sins; the LORD laid on Him the iniquity of us all).\
- The Son's vindication by the Father (resurrection, exaltation, justification of many).\
- 
\f0\b The Father's active role
\f2\b0  as the One who 
\f1\i delivers Him up
\f2\i0  (Isa 53:6, 10; Rom 8:32) and who 
\f1\i vindicates
\f2\i0  Him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What they do not establish:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 - They do not, by themselves, prove the Son's pre-existence or divinity. (Other passages, which we have already surveyed, do that \'97 Phil 2, John 17, John 8:58, Heb 1, etc.)\
- They speak of the Son as 
\f0\b the Servant
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b the Righteous One
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b the Man
\f2\b0  \'97 and at no point in these passages is He called "God."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What this confirms:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The pattern we have been building from the foundation upward holds firm:\
- 
\f0\b The Father is the One God
\f2\b0  \'97 who delivers up His Servant for our sins.\
- 
\f0\b The Son is the Servant of the LORD
\f2\b0  \'97 distinct from the Father, obedient unto death, vindicated by the Father.\
- 
\f0\b The Son's sufferings glorify the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 and the Father's pleasure prospers in the Servant's hand (Isa 53:10).\
This is the 
\f0\b Servant Christology
\f2\b0  of the earliest apostolic preaching (Acts 3:13, 26; 4:27, 30 \'97 all using 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u8150 \u962 
\f2\b0 ), and it is bound to the Father-Source / Son-Sent pattern we have established throughout.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Where We Now Stand\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Our study of the Person of Christ has now covered:\
1. 
\f0\b The One God, the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 Shema and Isa 44-46. \uc0\u10003 \
2. 
\f0\b The Son's pre-temporal glory and love with the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 John 17:5, 24; Phil 2:6; Heb 1:3. \uc0\u10003 \
3. 
\f0\b The Father created all things through the Son
\f2\b0  \'97 1 Cor 8:6; Col 1:16; Heb 1:2; John 1:3. \uc0\u10003 \
4. 
\f0\b The Son's coming in flesh, born of a woman
\f2\b0  \'97 Gen 3:15; Isa 7:14; Gal 4:4; Mic 5:2. \uc0\u10003 \
5. 
\f0\b The Son as the Father's Anointed Christ, His King at the right hand
\f2\b0  \'97 Ps 2; Ps 110; Matt 22; Acts 2; Heb 1, 5, 7. \uc0\u10003 \
6. 
\f0\b The Son's suffering, death, burial, and vindication as the Servant of the LORD
\f2\b0  \'97 Ps 22; Isa 53; Gospels; 1 Peter; Romans; Hebrews; Acts. \uc0\u10003 \
The arc is becoming complete: from the Father's pre-temporal love of His Son, through the goings-forth and incarnation, through the suffering and substitutionary death, to the resurrection vindication and exalted enthronement at the Father's right hand.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What Remains\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 To complete the study of the Person of Christ from the earliest prophecies to the concluding prophecies of the Apocalypse, the major areas still to examine include:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (A) The Son's exaltation and present session at the Father's right hand
\f2\b0  \'97 what He is doing 
\f1\i now
\f2\i0  as priest, intercessor, and ruler (Heb 7-10; Ps 110:1-4 fully).\

\f0\b (B) The Son's coming return
\f2\b0  \'97 the prophecies of His second appearing, His judgment of the living and the dead, and His reign (Daniel 7; Zechariah 12-14; Matt 24-25; Rev 19-22).\

\f0\b (C) The Son's final relation to the Father in the consummation
\f2\b0  \'97 including 1 Cor 15:24-28 (the Son delivering the Kingdom to the Father, that God may be all in all), which is one of the most theologically decisive passages on the Father-Son order at the end.\

\f0\b (D) The Son's titles and self-identifications in the Apocalypse
\f2\b0  \'97 the "I am" sayings of Revelation, the Lamb-on-the-Throne imagery, the Alpha and Omega designations, etc.\
Where would you have us go next?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Jesus\'92 Acts During His Ministry \'97 Part 1: Acts Fulfilling Prophecy\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Keep those in mind\'85 we will get to each one. But before we do, and in order to be thorough- let us also take note of Jesus\'92s acts during his ministry that tell us much of his person and fulfilled prophecy(s) both before and after his death, burial and resurrection.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is the proper next step \'97 for our study has so far moved largely through the 
\f1\i prophetic posits
\f2\i0  of the Son (OT prophecies and their NT fulfillments at His death/burial/resurrection), but we have not yet gathered the 
\f1\i acts of His ministry
\f2\i0  \'97 the things He 
\f0\b did
\f2\b0  and 
\f0\b said
\f2\b0  during His life that:\
1. 
\f0\b Reveal His Person
\f2\b0  (His authority, character, relation to the Father, self-identifications).\
2. 
\f0\b Fulfilled prophecy
\f2\b0  during His ministry (not just at His death).\
3. 
\f0\b Establish patterns
\f2\b0  that the Apocalypse and later prophecies will draw upon.\
Let me proceed under our refined modus operandi \'97 examining the whole counsel, giving the LXX/Greek and 1599 Geneva, citing all relevant cross-witnesses, and being honest about what is strictly established versus inferred.\
I will organize this by 
\f0\b categories of His ministerial acts
\f2\b0 , since chronology would scatter the patterns. We will examine:\
- 
\f0\b Part 1:
\f2\b0  Acts that fulfilled specific prophecies (His birth, ministry, and pre-Passion fulfillments)\
- 
\f0\b Part 2:
\f2\b0  His self-identifications (the "I am" sayings and titles He took)\
- 
\f0\b Part 3:
\f2\b0  Acts that revealed His authority (forgiving sins, commanding nature, raising the dead, giving the Spirit)\
- 
\f0\b Part 4:
\f2\b0  His relation to the Father (His words about His mission, His will, His subordination)\
- 
\f0\b Part 5:
\f2\b0  Post-resurrection acts that revealed His person and commissioned the Apostles\
This will be a substantial examination. Let us begin.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 # 
\f0\b PART 1 \'97 ACTS FULFILLING PROPHECY DURING HIS MINISTRY
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1.1 \'97 Born in Bethlehem of a Virgin\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 7:14, NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Therefore the Lord himself will give you a sign. Look, the virgin shall be with child and bear a son, and you shall name him Emmanouel. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 7:14 LXX, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Micah 5:2 LXX (5:1), NETS (already examined):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And you, O Bethleem 
\f1\i (Bethlehem)
\f2\i0 , house of Ephratha 
\f1\i (Ephrathah)
\f2\i0 , are very few in number to be among the thousands of Ioudas 
\f1\i (Judah)
\f2\i0 ; one from you shall come forth for me to become a ruler in Israel, and his goings forth are from of old, from days of yore 
\f1\i (long ago)
\f2\i0 . \'97 
\f0\b Micah 5:2 LXX (5:1), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 Matthew 1:22-23, 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And all this was done that it might be fulfilled which is spoken of the Lord by the Prophet, saying, Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bear a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which is by interpretation, God with us. \'97 
\f0\b Matthew 1:22-23, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Matthew 2:5-6 \'97 explicitly cites Micah 5:2 of Jesus\'92 birth in Bethlehem (already examined).\
Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  Matthew explicitly cites the LXX 
\f0\b \uc0\u7969  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i the virgin
\f2\i0 ) \'97 confirming the LXX reading against later attempts to render 
\f1\i "young woman."
\f2\i0  Per our maxim #1, the God-breathed text Jesus\'92 Apostles used reads 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0 .\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u956 \u956 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u965 \u942 \u955 
\f2\b0  is interpreted by Matthew as 
\f0\b \uc0\u924 \u949 \u952 \'92 \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "With us, God."
\f2\i0  The Son is "God with us" \'97 meaning, the One in whom God is present with His people. This is a profound title that we should not pass over but also not overstate \'97 it identifies Jesus as the embodied presence of God-with-His-people, not as a separate God.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1.2 \'97 Called Out of Egypt\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Hosea 11:1, NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 For Israel was an infant, and I loved him, and out of Egypt I recalled his children. \'97 
\f0\b Hosea 11:1 LXX (11:1 MT), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 Matthew 2:14-15, 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 So he arose and took the babe and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt, And was there unto the death of Herod, that that might be fulfilled, which is spoken of the Lord by the Prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son. \'97 
\f0\b Matthew 2:14-15, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Matthew identifies Jesus as 
\f0\b the Son
\f2\b0  whom the Father called out of Egypt \'97 fulfilling typologically what Israel-as-son had been (Israel = corporate son; Jesus = the True Son). This is 
\f0\b typology
\f2\b0 , not simple prediction-fulfillment. The Apostle, by inspiration, sees Jesus recapitulating Israel\'92s history.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1.3 \'97 The Voice in the Wilderness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 40:3, NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 A voice of one crying out in the wilderness: \'93Prepare the way of the Lord; make straight the paths of our God. \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 40:3 LXX, NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 Matthew 3:1-3, 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 For this is he of whom it is spoken by the Prophet Esaias, saying, The voice of him that crieth in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord: make his paths straight. \'97 
\f0\b Matthew 3:1-3, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Mark 1:2-3; Luke 3:4-6; John 1:23
\f2\b0  \'97 all identify John the Baptist as this voice, 
\f0\b preparing the way of the LORD
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of significant weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Isaiah 40:3 says: "Prepare the way of the LORD (\uc0\u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 )."
\f2\b0  The Gospels apply this to John the Baptist preparing the way of 
\f0\b Jesus
\f2\b0 . This is a strong identification: Jesus is the One 
\f1\i whose
\f2\i0  way is prepared, and the One being prepared for is called 
\f0\b \uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  in Isaiah.\
This does not automatically mean Jesus is identical with 
\f0\b YHWH
\f2\b0  \'97 but it does mean 
\f0\b the One coming in the LORD\'92s name and authority
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b bearing the LORD\'92s Name
\f2\b0  (cf. Phil 2:9: the Name above every name given to the Son). The way of the LORD is prepared because the LORD is acting 
\f1\i through
\f2\i0  His Christ.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 1.4 \'97 Galilee of the Nations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Isaiah 9:1-2 LXX (8:23-9:1), NETS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Do this first; do it quickly, O country of Zaboulon, the land of Nephthalime, and the rest who inhabit the seashore and beyond the Jordan, Galilee of the nations, the parts of Judea. O you people who walk in darkness, see a great light! O you who live in the country and in the shadow of death, light will shine on you! \'97 
\f0\b Isaiah 9:1-2 LXX (8:23-9:1), NETS
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cross-witness \'97 Matthew 4:14-16, 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Isaiah the Prophet, saying, The land of Zebulun, and the land of Nephthali by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles: The people which sat in darkness, saw great light: and to them which sat in the region, and shadow of death, light is risen up. \'97 
\f0\b Matthew 4:14-16, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus\'92 choice to base His ministry in Capernaum (Galilee of the Gentiles) is explicitly identified by Matthew as fulfilling Isaiah 9:1-2 \'97 
