\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of great weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Two NT witnesses
\f2\b0  (John 19 and Rev 1) bind 
\f0\b Zechariah 12:10
\f2\b0  directly to Jesus\'92 piercing on the cross and to His future return. This is one of the most important prophetic texts in our study because 
\f0\b it appears at both ends \'97 fulfilled at the crucifixion AND to be fulfilled at His return.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b A critical note on the Greek:
\f2\b0  The LXX of Zech 12:10 reads 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u960 \u953 \u946 \u955 \u941 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u949 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "they shall look upon Me"
\f2\i0  \'97 and 
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u972 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u960 \'92 \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "they shall mourn for Him."
\f2\i0  The shift from 
\f1\i "Me"
\f2\i0  to 
\f1\i "Him"
\f2\i0  within the same verse is striking. The LORD speaks (
\f1\i "they shall look upon Me"
\f2\i0 ) \'97 yet they mourn for 
\f1\i Him
\f2\i0  (a third person). This is the kind of Father-Son interplay we have been noting throughout: the LORD\'92s piercing is the piercing of His Sent One, and the mourning is for that Sent One.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

