\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus' confession before the high priest combines:
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b Psalm 110:1
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "sitting at the right hand of power"
\f2\i0 )\
- 
\f0\b Daniel 7:13
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i "coming on the clouds of heaven"
\f2\i0 )\
This is 
\f0\b Jesus' own claim of identity
\f2\b0 : He is the 
\f0\b Son of Man
\f2\b0  of Daniel 7, who will be enthroned and given universal dominion by the 
\f0\b Ancient of Days
\f2\b0  (the Father). His title 
\f0\b Son of Man
\f2\b0  is therefore not merely a humble human designation \'97 it is a claim to the 
\f0\b prophesied Heavenly Figure
\f2\b0  who will receive eternal dominion from the Father.\
This is also the 
\f0\b second witness alongside Psalm 110
\f2\b0  for the Son's enthronement at the Father's right hand.\

\f0\b An important note for our study:
\f2\b0  In Daniel 7, the 
\f0\b Son of Man
\f2\b0  is 
\f1\i brought before
\f2\i0  the 
\f0\b Ancient of Days
\f2\b0  \'97 He is 
\f1\i not
\f2\i0  the Ancient of Days. He is a 
\f1\i distinct figure
\f2\i0  who 
\f1\i receives
\f2\i0  dominion 
\f1\i from
\f2\i0  the Ancient of Days. This perfectly preserves our foundation: the Father is the One God on the throne; the Son receives all authority from Him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
