\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of considerable importance for our study\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Mark 13:32 is a critical text.
\f2\b0  Jesus explicitly says:\
- The 
\f0\b Son does not know
\f2\b0  the day or hour.\
- The 
\f0\b Father alone
\f2\b0  knows.\
This is Jesus' 
\f0\b own testimony
\f2\b0  that the Father has knowledge the Son does not have. 
\f0\b This is consistent with our entire foundation:
\f2\b0  the Father is the One supreme God, source of all things; the Son is the Sent One who operates in dependence and submission. He does not know what the Father has kept in His own authority (cf. Acts 1:7).\
This text alone is decisive against any reading that flattens the Son into being "of one substance" with the Father in such a way that He has all the Father's knowledge. 
\f0\b Per maxim #1, let God be true
\f2\b0  \'97 and Jesus Himself says 
\f0\b the Son does not know what the Father knows
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

