\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 5.1 \'97 Authentication of the Resurrection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The risen Jesus:\
- Appears to Mary Magdalene (John 20:11-18).\
- Appears to the disciples and shows His wounds (Luke 24:36-43; John 20:19-29).\
- Eats with His disciples (Luke 24:42-43; Acts 10:41) \'97 proving He is bodily, not a phantom.\
- Appears to 500 brethren at once (1 Cor 15:6).\
- Opens their understanding of the Scriptures (Luke 24:25-27, 44-47).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 5.2 \'97 The Great Commission\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Matthew 28:18-20:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 ... All power is given unto me, in heaven, and in earth. Go therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the Name of the Father, and the Son, and the holy Ghost, Teaching them to observe all things, whatsoever I have commanded you: and lo, I am with you alway, until the end of the world, Amen. \'97 
\f0\b Matthew 28:18-20, 1599 Geneva
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7960 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951  \u956 \u959 \u953  \u960 \u8118 \u963 \u945  \u7952 \u958 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "All authority 
\f3\b has been given
\f1\b0  to Me."
\f2\i0  Even after resurrection, the Son receives His authority 
\f0\b from
\f2\b0  the Father. The passive verb is decisive.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  The baptismal formula names 
\f0\b the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit
\f2\b0  \'97 though notice carefully that the 
\f0\b Name
\f2\b0  (singular: 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945 
\f2\b0 ) is one Name, not three. This text deserves more careful examination later in our study, but at minimum it establishes that the Father, the Son, and the Spirit are jointly involved in the disciple-making mission \'97 though Jesus does 
\f1\i not
\f2\i0  here teach a metaphysical doctrine of "three persons in one substance." He commands a baptism in a singular Name shared by the three.\
We should note, however, that the historical practice of the apostles in Acts is to baptize 
\f0\b "in the Name of Jesus Christ"
