\fs36 \cf0 1599 Geneva:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 "If therefore perfection had been by the Priesthood of the Levites (for under it the Law was established to the people) what needed it furthermore, that another Priest should rise after the order of Melchi-sedec, and not to be called after the order of Aaron? For if the Priesthood be changed, then of necessitie must there be a change of the Law. For he of whom these things are spoken, perteineth unto another tribe, whereof no man serued at the altar. For it is euident, that our Lord sprung out of Iuda, concerning the which tribe Moses spake nothing, touching the Priesthood. And it is yet a more euident thing, because that after the similitude of Melchi-sedec, there is risen up another Priest, Which is not made Priest after the Law of the carnal commandment, but after the power of the endlesse life. For he testifieth thus, Thou art a Priest for ever, after the order of Melchi-sedec."
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The Levitical priesthood could not bring perfection
\f2\b0  \'97 so a different priesthood was needed.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b Jesus is from Judah, not Levi
\f2\b0  \'97 He cannot be a priest after the Aaronic order. He must be a priest of a different order.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u956 \u953 \u957  \u950 \u969 \u8134 \u962  \u7936 \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u955 \u973 \u964 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "according to the power of an indestructible life."
\f2\i0  The new Priest holds priesthood 
\f0\b by the power of a life that cannot be destroyed
\f2\b0  \'97 that is, 
\f0\b the resurrected life of the Son
\f2\b0 . This is the key: His resurrection qualifies Him for this eternal priesthood.\

\f0\b (4) Cross-witness on Jesus' tribe \'97 Revelation 5:5:
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b 1599 Geneva:
\f2\b0  
\f1\i "...the Lion which is of the tribe of Judah..."
