\f2\b0  concerning Jesus' priesthood (citing Ps 110:4). The Father is the One swearing; the Son is the One sworn-to. Pattern preserved.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u961 \u949 \u943 \u964 \u964 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u948 \u953 \u945 \u952 \u942 \u954 \u951 \u962  \u947 \u941 \u947 \u959 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u7956 \u947 \u947 \u965 \u959 \u962  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "Jesus has become the guarantee of a better covenant."
\f2\i0  He is the 
\f1\i guarantor
\f2\i0  \'97 He stands between the parties as security.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u963 \u8180 \u950 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u8050 \u962  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u949 \u961 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u948 \u953 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He is able to save completely those who come to God through Him."
