Observe the critical preposition: 
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "through Him, to God [the Father]."
\f2\i0  We come 
\f0\b to God
\f2\b0  (the Father) 
\f0\b through Him
\f2\b0  (the Son). The pattern of 1 Cor 8:6 is 
\f1\i exactly
\f2\i0  preserved: the Father is the destination (
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 
\f2\b0 ); the Son is the way (
\f0\b \uc0\u948 \u953 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0 ).\

\f0\b (5)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u964 \u949  \u950 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u7952 \u957 \u964 \u965 \u947 \u967 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8182 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "always living to make intercession for them."
\f2\i0 \

\f0\b This is the Son's present, ongoing ministry.
\f2\b0  Right now, at this moment, the Son is 
\f0\b always living
\f2\b0  at the Father's right hand, 
\f0\b always interceding
\f2\b0  for those who come to the Father through Him. This is 
\f0\b what He is doing now.
\f2\b0 \
