\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 1 Timothy 2:5 is decisive for our entire study.
\f2\b0  Paul declares:\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7991 \u962  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i one God
\f2\i0  (the Father, per our foundation).\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7991 \u962  \u956 \u949 \u963 \u943 \u964 \u951 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i one Mediator
\f2\i0  \'97 between God and men.\
- 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the Man Christ Jesus
\f2\i0 .\

\f0\b The Mediator is the Man Christ Jesus.
\f2\b0  Paul, even after His exaltation, calls Him 
\f0\b \uc0\u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i Man
\f2\i0 . The mediation is 
\f0\b between God [the Father] and men
\f2\b0  \'97 and the Mediator stands between as 
\f0\b a Man
\f2\b0 .\
This is a critical text in our study because it preserves both:\
- 
\f0\b The Father as the One God
\f2\b0  (per the Shema and Isa 44-46).\
- 
\f0\b The Son as the exalted Man
\f2\b0  who mediates between God and men.\
The Son's 
\f0\b mediation
\f2\b0  at the Father's right hand is 
\f0\b as Man
\f2\b0  \'97 bearing the humanity He assumed in incarnation forever, now glorified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

