\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of foundational weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7957 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u954 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "stands"
\f2\i0  \'97 the Levitical priests 
\f0\b stand
\f2\b0  daily. 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u954 \u940 \u952 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "sat down"
\f2\i0  \'97 the Son 
\f0\b sat down
\f2\b0  after His one offering. The contrast is intentional: the seated Priest has finished His work; the standing priests have not.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u953 \u951 \u957 \u949 \u954 \u8050 \u962  \u7952 \u954 \u940 \u952 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8119  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "forever sat down at the right hand of God."
\f2\i0  The Son is enthroned forever \'97 
\f0\b at the right hand of God [the Father]
\f2\b0 . Psalm 110:1 is again confirmed.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8056  \u955 \u959 \u953 \u960 \u8056 \u957  \u7952 \u954 \u948 \u949 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7957 \u969 \u962  \u964 \u949 \u952 \u8182 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u959 \u7985  \u7952 \u967 \u952 \u961 \u959 \u8054  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8017 \u960 \u959 \u960 \u972 \u948 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u948 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "henceforth waiting until His enemies be made His footstool."
\f2\i0  Direct citation of Psalm 110:1.\
The Son is 
\f0\b waiting
\f2\b0  at the Father's right hand. This is His 
\f0\b present posture
\f2\b0  \'97 seated, interceding, waiting \'97 
\f0\b until the Father makes His enemies His footstool.
\f2\b0  The Father is the One who acts to subdue the enemies; the Son waits.\
This is a crucial detail for our study of His return: 
\f0\b the Father determines the timing
\f2\b0 ; the Son waits in expectation. This is consistent with Acts 1:7 (
\f1\i "It is not for you to know the times or the seasons, which the Father hath put in his own power"
\f2\i0 ) and Mark 13:32 (
\f1\i "neither knoweth the Son, but the Father"
\f2\i0 ).\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u956 \u953 \u8119  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u966 \u959 \u961 \u8119  \u964 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u969 \u954 \u949 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u953 \u951 \u957 \u949 \u954 \u8050 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u7937 \u947 \u953 \u945 \u950 \u959 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u965 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "by one offering He has perfected forever those who are being sanctified."
\f2\i0  
\f0\b One offering. Forever perfected.
\f2\b0  The work is finished.\
