\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What This Establishes About His Person \'97 Carefully\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The Son is, 
\f3\i now
\f0\i0 , a living Man
\f2\b0  \'97 exalted, glorified, but still 
\f0\b the Man Christ Jesus
\f2\b0  (1 Tim 2:5). He did not shed His humanity at the resurrection; He took it with Him into heaven.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b He bears the marks of His suffering even now.
\f2\b0  The risen Christ appeared with pierced hands and feet and side (John 20:25-27); the Lamb in the Apocalypse appears 
\f0\b as having been slain
\f2\b0  (Rev 5:6). The crucified Man is the enthroned Priest.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b He acts always in dependence on and submission to the Father.
\f2\b0  Even at the Father's right hand, He waits 
\f1\i for the Father to subdue His enemies
\f2\i0 . His enthronement does not erase the order: the Father is the One supreme God; the Son rules 
\f0\b at His right hand
\f2\b0  by His appointment.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b He is the only Mediator
\f2\b0  between the Father and humanity. No priest stands beside Him. No Mary, no saint, no apostle, no minister mediates between God and men \'97 
\f0\b only the Man Christ Jesus.
\f2\b0  This is critical doctrine, and it is firmly established.\

\f0\b (5)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b His ministry is 
\f3\i for us
\f0\i0 .
\f2\b0  Every act of His present session \'97 His appearing, His interceding, His waiting, His opening the way \'97 is 
\f0\b \uc0\u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 
\f2\b0  (
\f1\i on our behalf
\f2\i0 ). The Son's enthronement is not a private glory; it is an active ministry for those who come to the Father through Him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 A Critical Observation Preserving Our Foundation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Notice that throughout Hebrews 7-10, the Father remains 
\f0\b \uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i the God
\f2\i0  \'97 to whom:\
- The Son offered Himself (9:14: 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 
\f2\b0 ).\
- The Son sat down at His right hand (10:12: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u957  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8119  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0 ).\
- We come through the Son (7:25: 
\f0\b \uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 
\f2\b0 ).\
- The Father's house is overseen by the Son (10:21: 
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u959 \u7990 \u954 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0 ).\
- The Father swore the oath establishing the Son's priesthood (7:21).\
- The Father prepared the body for the Son's incarnation (10:5).\
- The Father's will is what the Son came to do (10:7-9).\
- The Father is the One who will make the Son's enemies His footstool (10:13).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The foundation we established at the beginning \'97 the Father as the One God \'97 is preserved unbroken throughout the Son's high-priestly ministry.
\f2\b0  The Son is never a rival to the Father, never an independent Deity, never "another God" \'97 He is 
\f0\b the appointed and beloved Son
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b the eternal Priest by the Father's oath
\f2\b0 , 
\f0\b the Mediator between God and men as the Man Christ Jesus
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 What Remains\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We have now completed (A). What remains, per your earlier direction:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 (B) The Son's coming return
\f2\b0  \'97 Daniel 7:13-14 fully expounded; Zechariah 12-14; Matthew 24-25; the Apocalypse's prophecies of His coming.\

\f0\b (C) The Son's final relation to the Father in the consummation
\f2\b0  \'97 1 Cor 15:24-28 (the Son delivering the Kingdom to the Father, "that God may be all in all"), which is perhaps the most theologically decisive passage on the Father-Son order at the end of all things.\

\f0\b (D) The Son's titles and self-identifications in the Apocalypse
\f2\b0  \'97 the I AM sayings of Revelation, the Lamb on the Throne, Alpha and Omega designations, and how these relate to and complete our study.\
Shall we now proceed to 
\f0\b (B)
\f2\b0  \'97 the Son's coming return \'97 beginning with 
\f0\b Daniel 7:13-14 fully expounded
\f2\b0  (since Jesus Himself cited this as the central image of His return before the high priest at Matt 26:64), and then moving through Zechariah 12-14 and the Olivet Discourse?\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Indeed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 We proceed to 
\f0\b (B) \'97 the Son's coming return
\f2\b0 .\
Per our refined modus operandi, we will:\
1. Begin with 
\f0\b Daniel 7
\f2\b0  \'97 the foundational vision Jesus cited as His own claim before the high priest.\
2. Examine 
\f0\b Zechariah 12-14
\f2\b0  \'97 the most extensive prophetic block on the Coming One's intervention in Jerusalem.\
3. Examine 
\f0\b Matthew 24-25 (the Olivet Discourse)
\f2\b0  \'97 Jesus' own direct teaching about His return.\
4. Cross-reference all other major NT witnesses (1 Thess, 2 Thess, 2 Peter, the Apocalypse) as they bear on the subject.\
We will let the whole counsel of the God-breathed Word establish what is to be established.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Daniel 7 \'97 The Son of Man before the Ancient of Days; the (B) Arc Opens\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 # 
\f0\b DANIEL 7 \'97 THE SON OF MAN BEFORE THE ANCIENT OF DAYS
\f2\b0 \
This is the foundational vision of the Son's coming reign, and it is the text Jesus Himself cited as His own (Matt 26:64; Mark 14:62).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Daniel 7:9-10, NETS (Old Greek):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 I kept watching until thrones were set, and an ancient of days sat, having a cloak like snow, and the tuft of hair on his head was like pure wool. The throne was like a flame of fire shooting out, and a stream of fire went out from before him. A thousand thousands were waiting on him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood attending him. And books were opened, and a court sat in judgment. \'97 
\f0\b Daniel 7:9-10, NETS (Old Greek)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 NETS\'92s Daniel carries Old Greek and Theodotion in parallel columns; the draft cites the LXX voice. Theodotion reads \'93and his clothing was white like snow, and the hair of his head was like pure wool; his throne was a flame of fire; its wheels were burning fire. A stream of fire drew in before him. A thousand thousands were serving him \'85 A court sat in judgment, and books were opened.\'94 
\f2\i0 (Theodotion, the parallel column)* \'97 the Old Greek print has \'93having a cloak like snow, and the tuft of hair on his head \'85 were waiting on him \'85 And books were opened, and a court sat in judgment.\'94 The draft\'92s observation Greek \uc0\u954 \u961 \u953 \u964 \u942 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u7952 \u954 \u940 \u952 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u946 \u943 \u946 \u955 \u959 \u953  \u7968 \u957 \u949 \u8180 \u967 \u952 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u957  carries the Theodotion order (a court sat, and books were opened).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of foundational weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u8182 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the Ancient of Days."
\f2\i0  This is 
\f0\b the Father
\f2\b0  \'97 the One God, the supreme Judge, enthroned in fire and surrounded by myriads of attendants. Per our foundation: 
\f0\b the Ancient of Days = the Father, the One God of the Shema and Isaiah 44-46.
\f2\b0 \

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u952 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u7952 \u964 \u941 \u952 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "thrones were set up"
\f2\i0  (plural). Multiple thrones \'97 preparing for the Son to be brought before the Father to receive His throne.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u961 \u953 \u964 \u942 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u7952 \u954 \u940 \u952 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u946 \u943 \u946 \u955 \u959 \u953  \u7968 \u957 \u949 \u8180 \u967 \u952 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the court sat, and the books were opened."
\f2\i0  The judgment scene is convened. This corresponds to 
\f0\b Revelation 20:11-12
\f2\b0  \'97 the great white throne judgment, where books are opened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Daniel 7:13-14, NETS (Old Greek) \'97 The Son of Man Coming\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Daniel 7:13-14, NETS (Old Greek):\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 I was watching in the night visions, and lo, as it were a son of man was coming upon the clouds of heaven. And he came as far as the ancient of days, and the attendants were present with him. And royal authority was given to him, and all the nations of the earth according to posterity, and all honor was serving him. And his authority is an everlasting authority, which shall never be removed\'97 and his kingship, which will never perish. \'97 
\f0\b Daniel 7:13-14, NETS (Old Greek)
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The same parallel columns; the seat prints the Old Greek. Theodotion reads \'93coming with the clouds of heaven \'85 and was presented to him. And to him was given the dominion and the honor and the kingship \'85 which will not be destroyed.\'94 
\f2\i0 (Theodotion, the parallel column)*. The draft\'92s observation Greek \uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8033 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8134 \u1606  is the Theodotion wording the Old Greek print renders \'93And he came as far as the ancient of days\'94 \'97 recorded when this passage was first seated (the Self-Identifications wave); no change now.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations of supreme importance for our study\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8033 \u962  \u965 \u7985 \u8056 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "as a Son of Man."
\f2\i0  The figure is described as 
\f0\b like a son of man
\f2\b0  \'97 i.e., 
\f0\b in the form of a Man.
\f2\b0  This corresponds with everything we have established about the Son: He is the exalted Man Christ Jesus (1 Tim 2:5; Heb 9:24).\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u957 \u949 \u966 \u949 \u955 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u959 \u8016 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "coming on the clouds of heaven."
\f2\i0  The mode of His coming is on the clouds \'97 fulfilled in:\
- Acts 1:9-11 (a cloud received Him; He shall so come)\
- Matt 24:30; 26:64\
- Rev 1:7\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8033 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8134 \u957 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He came as far as the Ancient of Days."
\f2\i0  The Son of Man 
\f0\b approaches
\f2\b0  the Ancient of Days. 
\f0\b He is brought 
\f3\i before
\f0\i0  the Ancient of Days \'97 He is 
\f3\i not
\f0\i0  the Ancient of Days.
\f2\b0  This is decisive for our foundation. Two distinct figures: the Father enthroned, and the Son of Man brought before Him.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u7952 \u958 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "authority was given to Him."
\f2\i0  
\f0\b By whom?
\f2\b0  The text's structure makes it clear: by the Ancient of Days (the Father). This is the same passive language we have seen throughout \'97 
\f0\b the Father gives; the Son receives.
\f2\b0  Matches Matt 28:18 (
\f1\i "All authority has been given to Me"
\f2\i0 ) \'97 explicitly received from the Father.\

\f0\b (5)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u964 \u8048  \u7956 \u952 \u957 \u951  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u947 \u8134 \u962 ... \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "all the nations of the earth... serving/worshipping Him."
\f2\i0  The verb 
\f0\b \uc0\u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u973 \u969 
\f2\b0  is the verb for 
\f0\b divine worship/service
\f2\b0  \'97 used of worship rendered to God. The Son of Man receives the divine service of all nations 
\f0\b by the Father's grant
\f2\b0 .\
This perfectly fulfills the pattern of Isa 45:23 \'97 
\f1\i "unto Me every knee shall bow"
\f2\i0  \'97 which Paul applies to Jesus in Phil 2:10-11, 
\f0\b "to the glory of God the Father."
\f2\b0  The worship rendered to the Son is by the Father's will and to the Father's glory.\

\f0\b (6)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u7952 \u958 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945  \u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 \u953 \u959 \u962 ... \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945  \u7973 \u964 \u953 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u956 \u8052  \u966 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u8135 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "eternal authority... a kingdom that shall not be destroyed."
\f2\i0  The Son's reign, granted by the Father, is everlasting.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

