\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, his disciples came unto him apart, saying, Tell us when these things shall be, and what sign shall be of thy coming, and of the end of the world.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The disciples ask three questions:\
1. When shall these things be? (referring to the destruction of the temple, v. 2)\
2. What shall be the sign of Your 
\f0\b \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 
\f2\b0  (presence, coming)?\
3. What shall be the sign of the end of the age?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i parousia
\f2\i0  \'97 is the technical term for the Son's coming. It means 
\f1\i "presence,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "arrival,"
\f2\i0  
\f1\i "royal visitation."
\f2\i0  It is used throughout the NT for His return.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Matthew 24:23-27 \'97 False Christs and the True Coming\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 Then if any shall say unto you, Lo, here is Christ, or there, believe it not. For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall show great signs and wonders, so that if it were possible, they should deceive the very elect. \'85 For as the lightning cometh out of the East, and is seen into the West, so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Jesus warns of 
\f0\b false Christs
\f2\b0  before His return. His true return will be 
\f0\b like lightning
\f2\b0  \'97 universally visible, unmistakable, undeniable. Not a secret coming. Not a private appearance. 
\f0\b Every eye shall see Him
\f2\b0  (Rev 1:7).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Matthew 24:29-31 \'97 The Sign of the Son of Man\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And immediately after the tribulations of those days, shall the sun be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of heaue 
\f1\i (heaven)
\f2\i0  shall be shake 
\f1\i (shaken)
\f2\i0 . And then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the kinreds 
\f1\i (kindreds)
\f2\i0  of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man come in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory. And he shall send his Angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect, from the four winds, and from the one end of the heavens unto the other.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1) The cosmic signs:
\f2\b0  sun darkened, moon without light, stars falling, powers shaken. This corresponds with:\
- 
\f0\b Isaiah 13:9-10 LXX
\f2\b0  (the Day of the LORD)\
- 
\f0\b Joel 2:31 LXX (3:4 LXX)
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "The sun shall be turned to darkness, and the moon to blood, before the great and notable day of the Lord comes."
\f2\i0  (NETS; cited by Peter in Acts 2:20).\
- 
\f0\b Revelation 6:12-14
\f2\b0  \'97 the sixth seal.\

\f0\b (2) "then shall all the kinreds 
\f3\i (kindreds)
\f0\i0  of the earth mourn"
\f2\b0  \'97 direct echo of 
\f0\b Zechariah 12:10-14
\f2\b0 , with Daniel 7's "coming on clouds." Jesus combines the same two texts He cited before the high priest.\

\f0\b (3) "His angels with a great trumpet"
\f2\b0  \'97 corresponds with:\
- 
\f0\b 1 Thess 4:16
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, and with the voice of the Archangel, and with the trumpet of God."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b 1 Cor 15:52
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "at the last trumpet."
\f2\i0 \
- 
\f0\b Rev 11:15
\f2\b0  \'97 the seventh trumpet.\

\f0\b (4) "Gather His elect from the four winds"
\f2\b0  \'97 the great gathering. The Son sends His angels to gather His chosen ones from the entire earth.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Matthew 24:36 \'97 Only the Father Knows\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 But of that day and hour knoweth no man, no not the Angels of heaven, but my Father only.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation of foundational weight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 This is Jesus' own testimony
\f2\b0 , identical to Mark 13:32:\
- The day and hour are known to 
\f0\b no man
\f2\b0 .\
- Not even 
\f0\b the angels.
\f2\b0 \
- 
\f0\b Not even the Son
\f2\b0  (in many manuscripts; the 1599 Geneva does not include "neither the Son" here, but Mark 13:32 does include it).\
- 
\f0\b Only the Father.
\f2\b0 \
Per our maxim #1 and the parallel in Mark 13:32 already established, 
\f0\b the Son does not know the day and hour; only the Father knows.
\f2\b0  This is decisive for our foundation: the Father remains the supreme One God who alone holds the times in His own authority (Acts 1:7 \'97 
\f1\i "the times, or the seasons, which the Father hath put in his own power"
\f2\i0 ).\
The Son's reign at the Father's right hand is real and supreme over creation \'97 but He does not possess the Father's exclusive sovereignty over the timing of the consummation. The Father is greater (John 14:28); the Father alone knows the day.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Matthew 25:31-46 \'97 The Son of Man Judges the Nations\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And when the Son of man cometh in his glory, and all the holy Angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory, and before him shall be gathered all nations, and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd separateth the sheep from the goats. And he shall set the sheep on his right hand, and the goats on the left. Then shall the King say to them on his right hand, Come ye blessed of my Father: take the inheritance of the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 (1)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u8005 \u964 \u945 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u7956 \u955 \u952 \u8131  \u8001  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u965  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u8131  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "When the Son of Man comes in His glory."
\f2\i0  This is the fulfillment of Daniel 7:13-14.\

\f0\b (2)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u952 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u965  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u951 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "He shall sit on His throne of glory."
\f2\i0  The Son of Man sits in judgment.\

\f0\b (3)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u959 \u7985  \u949 \u8016 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u951 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "the blessed of My Father."
\f2\i0  The blessing is from 
\f0\b the Father.
\f2\b0  Even at the judgment, the Son blesses those whom the Father has blessed.\

\f0\b (4)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \uc0\u954 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7969 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u956 \u945 \u963 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u951 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u946 \u959 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u965 
\f2\b0  \'97 
\f1\i "inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world."
\f2\i0  The kingdom was 
\f0\b prepared
\f2\b0  \'97 by the Father \'97 
\f0\b from the foundation of the world.
\f2\b0  The Father's eternal purpose is fulfilled.\

\f0\b (5)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b The Son judges the nations
\f2\b0 , separating sheep from goats. This corresponds with the authority given Him in John 5:22, 27 \'97 the Father has given all judgment to the Son.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
