\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 2 Thessalonians 1:7-10 \'97 The Revelation of the Lord Jesus\
\pard\pardeftab720\li831\fi-832\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf0 And to you which are troubled, rest with us, when the Lord Jesus shall show himself from heaven with his mighty Angels, In flaming fire, rendering vengeance unto them, that do not know God, and which obey not unto the Gospel of our Lord Jesus Christ, \'85 When he shall come to be glorified in his Saints, and to be made marvelous in all them that believe (because our testimony toward you was believed) in that day.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Observation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 The Lord Jesus comes 
\f0\b in flaming fire
\f2\b0  \'97 fulfilling Daniel 7:9-10 (the fire surrounding the Ancient of Days) but here belonging to the Son's return. 
\f0\b He renders vengeance on those who do not know God.
\f2\b0  The Father is the supreme God; rejection of the Father is the basis of judgment, executed by the Son.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
